    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "SQPOLL: a kernel thread polls the SQ, so submission needs no syscall at all.",
      "narration": "With SQPOLL a kernel thread polls the submission ring, so submitting needs no system call. It sleeps when idle and sets a wakeup flag.",
      "elements": [
        {
